### 2. [HIGH] Client-Side DoS: White Screen of Death (WSoD)

**Description:**
The "White Screen" is typically the result of an unhandled exception in the React rendering lifecycle that escapes the **Error Boundary**. In a 2026 context, this is often exploited as a **Client-Side Denial of Service**. If an attacker can trigger a specific UI state (e.g., via a malformed URL parameter or a malicious chat payload) that causes a crash, they can effectively lock users out of the application.

